      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'dat dinge gereël is en in 'n orde staan': 'in 'n orde staan' is not idiomatic Afrikaans in the glossary definition of 'georganiseerd'.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Nedersettings kom onder 'n middelpunt': Block heading: 'kom onder' calques English 'come under'; the body says 'onder 'n middelpunt ... begin val', so 'val onder' would match. Not proposed because a heading change may not be applicable.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Dié wat nie weggetrek het nie, het mettertyd deel van een ander groep ': 'een ander groep' is wooden and does not say which group (the newcomers of K2?). It cannot be fixed without guessing the intended content.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'So het die manier waarop die grond bewerk is, meer kompleks geword.': 'ingewikkelder' would be plainer at Grade 6, but 'kompleks' may be a CAPS term for this topic, so not proposed; the reviewer can decide.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Daar loop die Limpopo-rivier en dit vorm ons land se grens.': Reads as if the river is the whole national border; it is only part of the northern border. Wording a fix would add content, so it is flagged, not changed.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Al die mense wat saam leef en met mekaar te doen het.': This glossary term does not appear anywhere in the lesson text. The entry is also a fragment, where the other entries are full sentences."
